.01819],[128.75681,35.00726]]]},"wikidata":"Q16520","facts":{"population":{"value":3453198,"year":2018},"elevation":30,"officialArea":769.83,"website":"https://www.busan.go.kr/"},"summary":{"extract":"Busan, officially Busan Metropolitan City, is the second most populous city in South Korea, after Seoul; it has a population of over 3.3 million as of 2024. It is the economic, cultural and educational center of southeastern South Korea, with its port being South Korea's busiest and the sixth-busiest in the world. The surrounding \"Southeastern Maritime Industrial Region\" is South Korea's largest industrial area. The large volumes of port traffic and urban population in excess of 1 million makes Busan a Large-Port metropolis using the Southampton System of Port-City classification. As of 2025, Busan Port is the primary port in Korea and the world's sixth-largest container port.","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Busan_City_Haeundae_District_%2801%29.jpg/330px-Busan_City_Haeundae_District_%2801%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Busan"},"twins":["Q959","Q124739","Q181557","Q65","Q203308","Q1492","Q8678","Q26600","Q8686","Q11462","Q37100","Q33986","Q340","Q406","Q1297","Q1461","Q7903","Q656","Q1861","Q17151","Q169376","Q612","Q588451","Q5540","Q1854","Q38283","Q55630"],"climate":{"temp":[6.6,7.8,10.3,13.6,16.8,20.2,23.7,26.2,23.5,19.7,14.6,8.9],"rain":[39,58,87,138,148,177,287,224,187,81,54,41],"cloud":[55,60,57,58,62,73,73,66,67,54,51,52]}}